1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,160
Narrator: Scenario 27. Network and access.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:16,656
B: I can sign in through SSO, but the production console says access denied. My manager approved a read-only role yesterday for release verification.

3
00:00:17,256 --> 00:00:28,440
A: Authentication succeeded, but authorization appears to have failed. Please share the approval ticket and console error reference so we can verify the expected role.

4
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:39,216
B: The ticket is approved, and it names the production observer role. I can access staging, but I cannot open any production resource pages.

5
00:00:39,816 --> 00:00:50,952
C: I will check the identity group mapping and provisioning history. An approved request does not necessarily mean the console has received the membership update.

6
00:00:51,552 --> 00:01:02,520
A: Please compare the exact account identifier too. We have seen confusion when people use a contractor identity and an employee identity with similar names.

7
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:12,048
B: I am using the employee account listed in the request. Should I ask someone to lend me a working administrator session for the meeting?

8
00:01:12,648 --> 00:01:22,944
A: Keep access tied to your own identity and approved role. I can share the relevant read-only deployment evidence through the ticket while we investigate.

9
00:01:23,544 --> 00:01:35,136
C: The directory group is correct, but the console provisioning job rejected one mapping. I found a role name mismatch introduced in yesterday’s configuration update.

10
00:01:35,736 --> 00:01:45,576
A: Can you repair that mapping with the identity change owner and rerun provisioning? We should retain the original approval and record the correction.

11
00:01:46,176 --> 00:01:57,024
C: Yes. After the reviewed correction, I will confirm the assigned role in the audit log. Please start a new session once I notify you.

12
00:01:57,624 --> 00:02:09,000
B: I will test access at 15:00 UTC and confirm that production details are visible. I will also verify that write controls remain unavailable.

13
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:20,256
A: I will close the support ticket after those checks and attach the audit reference. The identity owner will separately track prevention of future mapping failures.
